WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Li Zicheng's army entered Beijing, and the Forbidden City was shrouded in the silence before dawn.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.760
The palace rooftops appeared faintly in the dim light, in a quiet that was hard to forget.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.640
The Chongzhen Emperor, Zhu Youjian, dressed in plain clothes, walked out of the palace gate alone.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.040
He looked back at the palace where he had lived for so many years, his eyes full of reluctance to leave.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:27.320
He slowly walked up the path on Coal Hill, as the pine trees swayed gently in the morning wind.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.280
The pines on both sides of the mountain path stood tall, as if silently seeing him off.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.720
The empty throne remained in the great hall, as an era quietly came to an end.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:43.360
A lone bell sounded in the distance, and the people bowed their heads in silent mourning.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.680
The bell's sound slowly faded into the morning mist, and calm returned to the streets.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.400
The sun rose over the city of Beijing, and the Ming dynasty, which had lasted more than two hundred years, came to an end.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.960
Golden sunlight spilled over the streets, and the people welcomed a new day.
